# Description:
# Launcher script for TestBox's BoxLang runner.
# It resolves this script's directory and executes:
#   system/runners/BoxLangRunner.bx
# passing through all CLI arguments unchanged.

# Get the path to the directory where this script is located.
# Deliberately kept relative (no `cd ... && pwd`): BoxLang 1.17.0+ forces
# absolute-looking paths passed to the engine to resolve against
# mappings/webroot instead of the OS filesystem, which can make an
# absolute entry-point path fail to self-resolve during the run. A
# relative path avoids that, and also keeps server.cli.executionPath
# pointing at the caller's working directory instead of this directory.
DIR="$( dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}" )"

# Go baby go!
boxlang "$DIR/system/runners/BoxLangRunner.bx" "$@"